    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d986">

                <pb facs="1337" n="1327" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg1327"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.4061 Motion Pictures/3–2945: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Atcheson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-03-29T16:00:00-04:00">March 29, 1945—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>509. The Hays Organization<anchor n="2" xml:id="d986-f1"/> has informed the
                    Department of the receipt by its company members of advices from Chungking that
                    film remittances for 1945 (ReEmbs 2717 of June 26, 1944<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d986-f2"/>) will be computed on a changed basis which will reduce
                    substantially the net earnings of American companies.</p>
                <p>The Hays Organization has requested the Embassy’s assistance in obtaining a more
                    reasonable arrangement in this matter and the Department would appreciate a
                    report in the premises by airgram indicating especially whether there was any
                    proper action which the Embassy was able to take in endeavoring to assist the
                    American companies.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
